id: VS-04
name: Risk Evaluation and Prioritisation
short_description: Turn assessed risks into prioritised decisions, funded treatments,
  and portfolio views (including concentrations/systemic risk).
owner: null
stakeholders:
- ExCo/Board, Risk Committee, Portfolio/Finance, Risk Owners
triggers:
- Completion of analysis, quarterly review, appetite breach, budget cycle.
inputs:
- Residual risk results (VS-03), appetite/criteria (VS-00), monitoring and control
  health (VS-06/VS-07), strategic priorities.
entry_criteria: ''
key_activities:
- 1) Evaluate residual vs appetite
- 2) Rank and cluster (themes/systemic/concentration)
- 3) Identify single points of failure and critical service exposures
- 4) Select response approach per risk
- 5) Build prioritised treatment backlog
- 6) Allocate owners and funding
- 7) Set review cadence by volatility
- 8) Publish portfolio decisions and actions.
decisions_and_gates: []
outputs:
- Top risk portfolio, heatmaps, concentration view, funded treatment backlog, escalation
  log, decision ledger.
exit_criteria: ''
metrics: 'Flow: decision lead time; throughput of funded treatments; WIP of unfunded
  high risks.<br>Performance: board clarity score; “one version of truth” disputes.<br>Risk:
  % high risks with funded plans; concentration indices; number of unresolved appetite
  breaches.'
source_file: docs\value-architecture\value-streams\VS-04-risk-evaluation-prioritisation.md
last_updated: '2026-02-01T12:57:43.598785Z'
